# Everything under tools/ is a local scratch harness and stays out of the repo.
*

# …EXCEPT the swiftcheck harness, which is not a scratch tool but a TEST: it
# asserts invariants of the SHIPPED app (the stale-K migration, the diagnostic
# run lock, the probe's duration bound) by compiling the real sources
# standalone, because the app has no test target.
#
# 🚨 It was written, run, and CLAIMED BY A COMMIT MESSAGE while `git ls-files`
# could not see it — a fresh clone had the claim and not the test. A blanket
# ignore hides a test exactly as well as it hides a binary. (2026-08-16)
!.gitignore
!swiftcheck/
!swiftcheck/*.swift
# …and the log scorers, for the same reason plus one more: THE INSTRUMENT AND
# ITS SCORER ARE ONE SYSTEM. A parser that lives only on one laptop gets
# rewritten from memory next time, and a scorer written AFTER a run gets tuned
# to that run's data. These are versioned beside the code they score.
!logscore/
!logscore/*.py
